,"links":[["Sawyer County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/wisconsin/sawyer-county"],["ARC or PLC in Sawyer County","/arc-plc/wisconsin/sawyer-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 14 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and January to February came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 on the middle, Sep-Oct and Oct-Nov each came in at 50% of normal. So far in 2026, May to June sits at 67% and June to July at 78% on the middle. Every grid shown had its driest year in 1976, with grids 31054 and 31055 down to 51% that year.</p>"}
